@startuml @ Journal

' This class is how the user interacts with the Journal and Entry classes.
class Program {
    + Main()
    + DisplayMenu()
}

' The Journal class is basically what does all the heavy lifting. It is what stores the Entries,
' saves them, displays entries, and adds them.
class Journal {
    - _entries : List<Entry>
    - _prompts : List<string>
    --
    + AddEntry()
    + Display()
    + GeneratePrompt()
    + SaveToFile()
    + LoadFromFile()
}

' The entry class will work under the Journal class.
' The Journal class will use Entry to generate a proper userinput entry
' and add that entry to the Journal entries list attribute.
class Entry {
    - _date : string
    - _prompt : string
    - _response : string
    --
    + Display()
}

Program --> Journal
Journal --> Entry

@enduml